  <heading level="2">Multiply Monomials</heading>
  <paragraph>Since a monomial is an algebraic expression, we can use the properties for simplifying expressions with exponents to multiply the monomials.</paragraph>
  <example number="10.26">
    <problem>
      <paragraph>Multiply: $${{({4x^{2}})}{({- 5x^{3}})}}.$$</paragraph>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <cell/>
            <cell>$$({4x^{2}}){( - 5x^{3}})$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Use the Commutative Property to rearrange the factors.</cell>
            <cell>$$4 \cdot {(-5)} \cdot x^{2} \cdot x^{3}$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Multiply.</cell>
            <cell>$$- 20x^{5}$$</cell>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </solution>
  </example>
